# Sifrah Development Rules for Cursor & AI Agents

# General Guidelines
- Sifrah is a multi-tier MLM & HealthTech platform.
- Frontends: Vue.js in `app/` (Capacitor for Android/iOS) and `admin/` (Vercel).
- Backend: Monolithic Node.js/Next.js in `server/` running on DigitalOcean (`68.183.125.105`) via PM2.
- Heavy calculation: Golang 1.20 in `cierre_engine/` using Goroutines for sub-15s massive bonus settlement.
- Database: MongoDB 6.x hosted on dedicated AWS EC2 in Ohio (`ec2-18-220-240-71.us-east-2.compute.amazonaws.com:27017`).

# Critical Domain Rules
1. WALLET SAFETY: Never update user wallet balances directly without passing through `server/components/wallet-lock.js`. Prevent double-spending with mutex locking.
2. DYNAMIC COMPRESSION: When computing MLM bonuses, inactive distributors must be bypassed and their volume passed to the next qualified upline.
3. MEDICAL GUARDRAILS: In `server/components/ai-catalog.js`, never bypass `evaluateMedicalGuardrails`. Emergencies (infarcts, tumors, severe bleeding) must trigger medical triage warnings and block supplement sales.
4. SAFE MONGO QUERIES: Never execute unqualified drop or delete operations. Treat AWS MongoDB with extreme care.
5. REFERRAL TRACKING: All product recommendations generated by the AI assistant must retain the distributor's referral code (`refCode`).

# Commands
- Server Dev: `cd server && npm run dev`
- App Dev: `cd app && npm run serve`
- Admin Dev: `cd admin && npm run serve`
- Go Engine: `cd cierre_engine && go build -o cierre_bin main.go && go test ./...`
